# Line endings are part of this project's test data.
#
# Several tests parse a file and assert on character offsets into it -
# core/src/test/scripts/nosecurity/parserapi.js reads its own source and prints
# every node's startPosition/endPosition, and the treeapi tests do the same for
# the files they parse. A CRLF checkout adds one character per line, so every
# offset shifts and the .js.EXPECTED comparison fails: on Windows, parserapi.js
# reported endPosition 1138 where the expected file says 1109, one byte for each
# of the 29 line endings in between.
#
# So the whole tree is normalised to LF in the working tree on every platform,
# not merely in the repository. There are no .bat or .cmd files here, and the
# shell scripts need LF anyway.
#
# NOTE for an existing Windows checkout: this file only governs what git writes
# out. A tree already checked out with CRLF stays that way until it is
# renormalised, and `git checkout -- .` alone will not do it - git's stat cache
# considers the files unchanged and skips them. This does:
#
#     git add --renormalize .
#     git commit -m "normalise line endings"      (or reset, if there is nothing to commit)
#     git rm --cached -r .
#     git reset --hard
#
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and left exactly as it is.
*.png binary
